{"kind":"request","text":"Claude: let gs review read its report from a file.\n\nLong review reports are formatted text: headings, tables, quoted findings, code. Passing them through --text on the command line means shell quoting, escaped newlines and truncated pastes, and the workroom then holds a mangled verdict. Add --text-file PATH to gs review, taking the report from that file as the verdict text, exactly as --text would. Do the same on gs state, which files reports and asserts that have the same problem. The two flags are exclusive; exactly one is required where --text is required today. Keep it small: no stdin, no templating, no change to how the text is signed or displayed.","body":{"branch":"request/review-text-file","conditions":"1. gs review --text-file PATH files the file's contents as the report text, byte for byte apart from trailing whitespace, and gs state --text-file PATH does the same for statement text. 2. Giving both --text and --text-file, or neither where text is required, or an empty or blank file, or an unreadable path, is refused before anything is signed, with a message naming the flag. 3. Tests cover the accepted and each refused case for both commands. 4. docs/reference/gs/review.md and docs/reference/gs/state.md document the flag. 5. Independent review by codex, ratified, then landed on main and pushed.","target_head":"8e77fc25519b62b76ec89b0a2fb1311d92fa0baa","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8","to":"a5d35aa7e4799472a208663d7f024917442bd513929f9eccf450628ccf70095d"}}